From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Thu, 20 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: add the elimination body and visit each living duelist
 once

Phase 2, task T5B. Nobody calls field::eliminate for n > 2 until the loss checks (T5A) land.

New code (1 function and 1 helper, field.cpp): eliminate(p, reason). It returns at once (no flag, no message) when
n_duelists == 2 or p is already out. For n > 2 it sets the flag and sends MSG_DUELIST_ELIMINATED (200), sets force_turn_end when p
is the turn player, drops p's entries from the pending chain lists (new_fchain, new_ochain and their _s, _b, _h
forms, new_chains, quick_f_chain) and drops delayed quick effects of p's cards, rolls back or cancels attacks
that involve p, and removes the cards. Cards p owns leave the game with MSG_REMOVE_CARDS (at most 255 per message,
Xyz materials first). A card p controls and does not own goes to its owner's Graveyard with send_to (REASON_RULE).
Materials of other duelists under a removed Xyz monster go to their owner's Graveyard. The none id for reason
players is DUELIST_NONE, and send_to gets the owner as the target duelist (PLAYER_NONE is duelist 2 when n > 2). Equip links are cut and
equip cards of others that lose their target are destroyed. Effects of p's cards that reset at a phase end are
removed. The declaration in field.h takes the new reason argument. The message ids 200 to 202 are added to common.h.

Sites in stock code (5 kinds, 11 places):
- SolveChain case 2: the link of an eliminated duelist gets MSG_CHAIN_DISABLED and no operation (n > 2 only).
- Adjust step 14: no attack target and the defender is gone gives attack_rollback (n > 2 only).
- Loops that stepped next_in_turn_order n_duelists times and visited a living duelist twice after an
  elimination: adjust_self_destroy_set (field.cpp), TrapMonsterAdjust case 4 (operations.cpp), SelectCounter
  (playerop.cpp), Adjust steps 2, 10, 11 and 12 (processor.cpp). With n > 2 each starts at the first living
  duelist from the turn player and stops when it is back there.

With 2 duelists: every changed statement is behind n_duelists > 2 or n_duelists == 2, so the stock text runs
unchanged. eliminate does nothing. No new message, random call or Lua call for n == 2.

Left for other tasks: the calls of eliminate and the loss checks (T5A), Debug.EliminateDuelist (T5A), the
battle_defender value and the attack target union (T4), the response order (T3), the disabled zones (T6).

